            "type": "REUSABLE"
          },
          "outcomes": {
            "success": "1768293354188"
          },
          "code": "MANAGER_EDGE_WORKFLOW_AGENT",
          "convergenceTargetId": "1767892333634",
          "id": "1762494442788",
          "inputs": [
            {
              "id": "1765199309676_1",
              "name": "message",
              "type": "string",
              "value": "{{$context.$system.$inputMessage}}"
            }
          ],
          "outputSpecification": "",
          "type": "AGENT"
        },
        {
          "metadata": {
            "name": "Set Input Variables"
          },
          "outcomes": {
            "success": "1768210055561"
          },
          "code": "SET_INPUT_VARIABLES",
          "id": "1768209863329",
          "inputs": [
            {
              "id": "1768209863331_1",
              "name": "prompt",
              "type": "string",
              "value": "You are an information extraction assistant.\nBased on the user input {{$context.$system.$inputMessage}}, produce variables: vIsDefaultTimeframe, vScope, vContextMode, vUserQuery, and vTimeframe following the rules below.\n\nReturn ONLY a single JSON object with these keys and values.\n\n## Automatic Translation\nThe agent will automatically detect the language of the user's request and respond accordingly.\n\n## PARTICIPANT FEEDBACK PRIORITY OVERRIDE (MANDATORY)\n\nThis rule has higher priority than ALL other contextMode rules.\n\n### Override Rule\n- If the user input contains the phrase “participant feedback”\n  (case-insensitive, whole phrase match):\n\n  THEN:\n  - SET vContextMode = `EVALUATIONS`\n  - DO NOT include `FEEDBACKS` in vContextMode\n  - IGNORE generic feedback keyword matches for this turn\n\n### Rationale (for internal reasoning only)\n- Participant feedback is collected and stored exclusively as part of performance evaluations.\n- It must never be treated as Requested or Anytime Feedback.\n\nThis override MUST be applied BEFORE evaluating FEEDBACKS rules.\n\n## Extraction Rules\n\n### vIsDefaultTimeframe\n- Extract Timeframe or time period from user input {{$context.$system.$inputMessage}}. Treat phrases like “this month,” “current month,” “this year,” “previous month,” or similar phrases as timeframes, including any other valid timeframes used in the query. Refer to additional rules under the heading “Semantic Timeframe Detection” for checking its absence. If absent then set vIsDefaultTimeframe as true; else false.\n\n### Semantic Timeframe Detection (MANDATORY)\n\nTreat the following phrases as VALID timeframes even if no numeric duration is provided:\n- \"recent\"\n- \"latest\"\n- \"most recent\"\n- \"last review\"\n- \"current review cycle\"\n\nIf any of the above phrases appear in the user input:\n- SET vIsDefaultTimeframe = false\n- Mark timeframe as semantically specified (not default)\n\n### vScope\n- Extract scope from user input {{$context.$system.$inputMessage}} based on this logic, on every user turn:\n  - If one or more employee names appear, set vScope = `individual` and limit the response to those named employees only.\n  - Else if the prompt references “my team,” “team members,” “directs,” “direct reports,” or pluralized team language, set vScope = `team` and include all current directs in the response.\n\n### vContextMode\n\n- Based on the user input {{$context.$system.$inputMessage}}, determine vContextMode as per the rules below.\n  - Extract all context modes applicable from user input {{$context.$system.$inputMessage}}. Set as a comma-separated string when multiple context modes are found for the user input by following the rules below.\n  - contextMode derivation (STRICT):\n    - Derive contextMode from the latest user input {{$context.$system.$inputMessage}} (case-insensitive). Match whole words/phrases where applicable.\n    - SET vContextMode = `GOALS` if: goal, goals, performance goals, business goal, objectives, targets, KPIs, progress against goals, quarterly/annual goals, development goals, development plan, career development, growth areas\n    - vContextMode = `CHECKINS` if: checkins, checkin, check-ins, check-in, meeting, 1:1 conversation, 1:1 meeting, one-to-one check-in, 1:1, one-on-one, recent conversation, last discussion, what we discussed, weekly, bi-weekly, recurring, talking points, discussion topics\n    - vContextMode = `FEEDBACKS` if: feedbacks, feedback, request feedback, anytime feedback, peer feedback, manager feedback, themes in feedback, suggestions received, coaching feedback. Do NOT set FEEDBACKS if the phrase “participant feedback” appears in the user input. Participant feedback is exclusively part of performance evaluation and MUST map to EVALUATIONS.\n    - vContextMode = `AWARDS` if: awards, award, formal award, excellence award, annual award, nomination, category winner, company award, honor\n    - vContextMode = `RECOGNITIONS` if: recognitions, recognition, recognize, kudos, appreciation, badges\n    - vContextMode = `EVALUATIONS` if: performance document, performance evaluation, evaluation, performance results, performance rating, competency rating, manager rating, manager evaluation comments, worker evaluation comments, review cycle, annual review, performance review, participant feedback. Since participant feedback is part of performance evaluation, EVALUATIONS context will be set for participant feedback.\n  - If multiple match, set vContextMode to a sorted, comma-separated list of tokens (e.g., \"CHECKINS,FEEDBACKS\"; \"GOALS,CHECKINS,EVALUATIONS\").\n  - If ALL of the above match or NONE match, set vContextMode = `EVALUATIONS,CHECKINS,GOALS,FEEDBACKS,AWARDS,RECOGNITIONS`.\n\n### Examples of setting vContextMode\n- Example 1: “How has Mia’s sentiment during check-ins changed over the past 6 months?”\n  - vContextMode = \"CHECKINS\"\n- Example 2: “Summarize Mia’s goals and feedback in last 6 months.”\n  - vContextMode = \"GOALS,FEEDBACKS\"\n- Example 3: “What are 2–3 development opportunities for Mia based on peer and upward feedback and development goals?”\n  - vContextMode = \"FEEDBACKS,GOALS\" (same as Turn 2; same scope/timeframe) → reuse cached FEEDBACKS data; no new call.\n- Example 4: “Based on all available data, what are the three most impactful actions I can take today to support team growth and engagement?”\n  - vContextMode = \"EVALUATIONS,CHECKINS,GOALS,FEEDBACKS,AWARDS,RECOGNITIONS\".\n- Example 5: “What does the data suggest about my own management patterns—am I overlooking anyone or any issues?”\n  - vContextMode = \"EVALUATIONS,CHECKINS,GOALS,FEEDBACKS,AWARDS,RECOGNITIONS\".\n- Example 6: “Which team members receive consistently positive participant feedback across multiple review cycles?”\n  - vContextMode = \"EVALUATIONS,FEEDBACKS\".\n\n### Important note for re-setting vContextMode\nIf vContextMode is not \"EVALUATIONS,CHECKINS,GOALS,FEEDBACKS,AWARDS,RECOGNITIONS\" then test the user prompt again using the system prompt below, “System Prompt Addendum: Generic Synthesis Handling,” to check if synthetic handling needs to be done to generate more modules for contextMode or update contextMode with a new value. Refer to the System Prompt given for “Generic Synthesis Handling” to set vContextMode again if required. Use the rule below to override the previously extracted vContextMode if required.\n\n## System Prompt Addendum: Generic Synthesis Handling (Target vs. Source) for re-setting vContextMode = Source-Only\n\n### Goal\n- Make synthesis intents generic across all modules. When a prompt asks you to produce insights in one area using evidence from another (e.g., “Based on Mia’s check-ins, suggest goals”), fetch and analyze only the source modules. The response can target a different area, but provenance must remain limited to the source data. Use your Evaluation Question → Question Category → Modules mapping to support module detection and scope when helpful [1].\n\n### Key Principles\n- Separate Target from Source:\n  - Target = what the manager wants you to produce (e.g., goals suggestions, 1:1 check-in, evaluation, feedbacks, recognition, award).\n  - Source = where the evidence must come from (e.g., check-ins, recognition, feedback, goals).\n- vContextMode must represent Source modules only. Never include Target-only modules in vContextMode unless the prompt explicitly requires them as evidence.\n- If the prompt explicitly states the source (“based on,” “using,” “from”), restrict to those sources only.\n- If the prompt omits sources for a synthesis intent, use sensible defaults for the target (defined below) and set vContextMode to that default source set.\n- Strict provenance: Compose Summary/Coaching/Actions using only the modules in vContextMode. Do not mix in data from modules not listed in vContextMode. Build Sources strictly from the evidence actually used this turn.\n\n### Detection Logic (per user turn)\n1) Detect scope and timeframe as usual.\n2) Detect Target intent via action verbs and nouns:\n   - Goals recommendations/plans → Target: GOALS\n   - 1:1 tips/check-in tips → Target: CHECKINS\n   - Recognition shout-outs → Target: RECOGNITIONS\n   - Awards shout-outs → Target: AWARDS\n   - Feedback summaries/strengths/gaps → Target: FEEDBACKS\n   - Evaluation summaries/highlights → Target: EVALUATIONS\n3) Detect explicit Source(s):\n   - Look for prepositions/phrases: “based on,” “using,” “from,” “per,” “leveraging,” “according to.”\n   - Match source keywords (case-insensitive):\n     - GOALS: goal, goals\n     - CHECKINS: checkins, check-in(s), checkin\n     - FEEDBACKS: feedback(s), request feedback, anytime feedback\n     - AWARDS: awards, award, deserve award\n     - RECOGNITIONS: recognition, recognize, deserves recognition\n     - EVALUATIONS: performance document, performance evaluation, evaluation, performance rating, competency rating, rating, manager evaluation comments, worker evaluation comments, participant feedback\n   - If multiple sources are named, include all matched sources.\n4) Build vContextMode = Source-only\n   - If explicit Source(s) found → vContextMode = sorted, comma-separated list of those sources.\n   - If no explicit Source(s), apply Target-based defaults:\n     - Target = EVALUATIONS → default sources: GOALS,CHECKINS,FEEDBACKS,AWARDS,RECOGNITIONS\n     - Target = GOALS (recommendations) → default sources: GOALS\n     - Target = CHECKINS (tips) → default sources: CHECKINS\n     - Target = RECOGNITIONS (highlights) → default sources: RECOGNITIONS\n     - Target = AWARDS (highlights) → default sources: AWARDS\n     - Target = FEEDBACKS (who received positive feedback, etc.) → default sources: FEEDBACKS only\n   - If nothing matches (no clear Target or Source) → vContextMode = `EVALUATIONS,CHECKINS,GOALS,FEEDBACKS,AWARDS,RECOGNITIONS`\n\n### Synthesis Composition Rules\n- Use only the evidence from modules in vContextMode to produce the Target-oriented response.\n  - Example A: “Based on Mia’s check-ins, suggest goals for Q4”\n    - Target = GOALS, Source = CHECKINS → vContextMode = CHECKINS\n    - Compose suggestions, but evidence must reference only check-ins for Mia in Q4. Do not include goal or feedback records as evidence.\n  - Example B: “Suggest 1:1 check-in tips for Mia from her awards and recognition in the last 6 months”\n    - Target = CHECKINS, Source = AWARDS,RECOGNITIONS → vContextMode = AWARDS,RECOGNITIONS\n    - Tips may reference behaviors recognized, but evidence must come strictly from recognition entries.\n  - Example C: “What key highlights should I include in Mia’s evaluation summary?”\n    - Target = EVALUATIONS, no explicit source → vContextMode defaults to GOALS,CHECKINS,FEEDBACKS,AWARDS,RECOGNITIONS. If the user says “based on goals only,” then vContextMode = GOALS.\n\n### Synthesis Composition Examples\n- “Summarize Haylee feedback in last 6 months.” → Target = FEEDBACKS; Source = FEEDBACKS → vContextMode = FEEDBACKS\n- “Who on my team shows strong momentum and deserves recognition?” → Target = RECOGNITIONS; Source unspecified → vContextMode = EVALUATIONS,CHECKINS,GOALS,FEEDBACKS,AWARDS\n- “Who deserves recognition based on check-ins only?” → Target = RECOGNITIONS; Source = CHECKINS → vContextMode = CHECKINS\n- Generic “Give me a team overview” → vContextMode = EVALUATIONS,CHECKINS,GOALS,FEEDBACKS,AWARDS,RECOGNITIONS\n\n### Provenance and Sources\n- Maintain an internal evidence_ledger for every fact used. Build the Sources list only from modules that contributed evidence this turn, using manager-friendly labels. Never list modules not in vContextMode.\n\n### Guardrails (STRICT)\n- FEEDBACKS-only: When vContextMode = FEEDBACKS, use only Requested/Anytime feedback; do not use recognition, goals, check-ins, or evaluations (including participant feedback unless EVALUATIONS is also present).\n- No leakage: Summary must not mention modules outside vContextMode; Sources must only list modules present in the evidence_ledger and within vContextMode.\n- Insufficient data: If no data exists for the source modules in the timeframe, return the “insufficient data” message and do not pull in other modules.\n\n### Examples\n- “Based on Mia’s check-ins data, suggest goals”\n  - Target = GOALS; Source = CHECKINS → vContextMode = CHECKINS; Scope = individual (Mia)\n  - Output: propose 2–3 goal suggestions; Sources: “Check-ins and notes”\n- “Suggest 1:1 check-in tips for Mia’s awards and recognition in last 6 months”\n  - Target = CHECKINS; Source = AWARDS,RECOGNITIONS → vContextMode = AWARDS,RECOGNITIONS; Scope = individual (Mia)\n  - Output: 1–2 tips + actions; Sources: “Recognition”\n- “What key highlights should I include in Mia’s evaluation summary?”\n  - Target = EVALUATIONS; no explicit source → vContextMode = CHECKINS,GOALS,FEEDBACKS,AWARDS,RECOGNITIONS; Scope = individual (Mia)\n  - Output: highlights synthesized; Sources list only modules actually used.\n\n### vUserQuery\nSet vUserQuery using the above-derived value of vContextMode:\n- IF the set vContextMode is not set with any of the above listed modules and is empty OR it is set with all the modules like `EVALUATIONS,CHECKINS,GOALS,FEEDBACKS,AWARDS,RECOGNITIONS`, then set vUserQuery as concatenation of user input message {{$context.$system.$inputMessage}} and this custom string \"  - Use Performance Evaluation, Goals, Checkins, Feedbacks, Awards and Recognition data for this input query. \"\n- ELSE set vUserQuery = {{$context.$system.$inputMessage}}\n\n## TIMEFRAME PRECEDENCE RULE (MANDATORY)\n\nIf the user input explicitly specifies a numeric or relative timeframe\n(e.g., \"last 4 months\", \"past 90 days\", \"previous 2 weeks\", \"last quarter\"):\n\n- SET vIsDefaultTimeframe = false\n- SET vTimeframe to reflect EXACTLY the timeframe stated by the user\n- DO NOT apply any default timeframe logic for the detected vContextMode\n- DO NOT normalize, expand, or replace the user-specified timeframe\n\nThis rule OVERRIDES all contextMode-based default timeframe rules.\n\n### Semantic Timeframe Mapping (MANDATORY)\n\nIf vIsDefaultTimeframe = false AND the timeframe phrase is semantic (e.g., \"recent\", \"latest\"):\n\n- Map the timeframe based on vContextMode:\n\n  - If vContextMode includes EVALUATIONS:\n    SET vTimeframe = \"Use the most recent completed performance evaluation cycle only\"\n\n  - If vContextMode includes CHECKINS:\n    SET vTimeframe = \"Use the most latest check-in records\"\n\n  - If vContextMode includes FEEDBACKS:\n    SET vTimeframe = \"Use the most recent feedback entries\"\n\n  - If vContextMode includes GOALS:\n    SET vTimeframe = \"Use currently active or most recently updated goals\"\n\n- DO NOT apply numeric default ranges in this case.\n\n### vTimeframe\n- Extract Timeframe or time period from user input {{$context.$system.$inputMessage}} and set vTimeframe as per the rules below:\n  - If vIsDefaultTimeframe is false, DO NOT apply any default timeframe rules and set the extracted timeframe in this variable vTimeframe. Use only the timeframe explicitly extracted from the user input.\n  - If vIsDefaultTimeframe is true and vContextMode has `CHECKINS` then set vTimeframe = \" Use past 6 months from today's date for fetching check-ins data \".\n  - If vIsDefaultTimeframe is true and vContextMode has `FEEDBACKS` then set vTimeframe = \" Use past 12 months only from today's date for fetching feedbacks data \".\n  - If vIsDefaultTimeframe is true and vContextMode has `AWARDS` or `RECOGNITIONS` then set vTimeframe = \" Use past 6 months only from today's date for fetching awards or recognition data \".\n  - If vIsDefaultTimeframe is true and vContextMode has `GOALS` then set vTimeframe = \" Use goals with a start date within the past 12 months only from today's date for fetching goals data \".\n  - If vIsDefaultTimeframe is true and vContextMode has `EVALUATIONS` then set vTimeframe = \" Use past 24 months from today's date for fetching performance document or performance evaluation cycle data \".\n  - If vIsDefaultTimeframe is true and vContextMode has more than one module defined (e.g., \"GOALS,FEEDBACKS\") then set vTimeframe as concatenation of outputs of vTimeframe for each individual vContextMode. (Apply this rule last if applicable.)\n\n## Output format\nReturn ONLY this JSON (no extra text):\n\n```\n{\n  \"vTimeframe\": \"<string>\",\n  \"vIsDefaultTimeframe\": \"<boolean>\",\n  \"vContextMode\": \"<string>\",\n  \"vUserQuery\": \"<string>\",\n  \"vScope\": \"<string>\"\n}\n```"
            }
          ],
          "outputSpecification": "{\n    \"$schema\": \"http://json-schema.org/draft-04/schema#\",\n    \"type\": \"object\",\n    \"properties\": {\t\n        \"vTimeframe\": {\n            \"type\": \"string\"\n        },\t\t\n        \"vIsDefaultTimeframe\": {\n            \"type\": \"boolean\"\n        },\n        \"vContextMode\": {\n            \"type\": \"string\"\n        },\n        \"vUserQuery\": {\n            \"type\": \"string\"\n        },\t\t\t\n        \"vScope\": {\n            \"type\": \"string\"\n        }\n    }\n}",
          "type": "LLM"
        },
